{title: The Lord's My Shepherd}
{artist: Scottish Psalter · Crimond}
{key: F}
{time: 3/2}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
The [F]Lord's my [Bb]shepherd, [F]I'll not [Dm]want: he [Gm]makes me [C]down to [F]lie
in [Bb]pastures [F]green; he [Bb]leadeth [F]me the [Gm]quiet [C]waters [F]by.

Verse 2
My [F]soul He [Bb]doth [F]restore again, And [Gm]me to [C]walk doth [F]make.
Within [Bb]the [F]paths of [Bb]blessedness, E'en [F]for His [Gm]Own [C]Name's [F]sake;

Verse 3
Yea, [F]though I [Bb]walk [F]in death's [Dm]dark vale, Yet [Gm]will I [C]fear no [F]ill,
For [Bb]Thou [F]art with me, [Bb]and Thy [F]rod And [Gm]staff [C]me comfort [F]still;

Verse 4
My [F]table Thou hast furnished [Dm]well In [Gm]presence [C]of my [F]foes;
My [Bb]head [F]Thou dost [Bb]with oil [F]anoint, And [Gm]my [C]cup [F]overflows;

Verse 5
Goodness [F]and [Bb]mercy [F]all my days [Gm]Will surely follow [F]me:
And [Bb]in [F]my Father's [Bb]heart always [F]My dwelling [Gm]place [C]shall [F]be;
